1. WEB SOURCE ANALYSIS (read end-to-end before writing native code)
------------------------------------------------------------
  EmptyStateThreshold.tsx is a PURE presentational component. Its only "data source" is
  `useTranslation` (i18n) — no queries, no async, so it has NONE of the loading/error/stale/offline
  axes the data-bound leaves carry. It IS the non-error empty state a section shows until it reaches
  useful scale (e.g. a heatmap needs >= 30 sessions). The render branches it DOES have are all
  reproduced:
    - itemNoun: provided vs. default  (web `itemNoun ?? t('emptyState.threshold.defaultItem','items')`)
    - message:  composed vs. override (web `message ?? defaultMessage`)
    - description: present vs. absent (web `description && <p>`)
    - count-vs-threshold range (0 / partial / at / over)
  i18n keys reproduced verbatim (the only two t() calls in the source):
    - emptyState.threshold.defaultItem = "items"
    - emptyState.threshold.message     = "Need at least {{threshold}} {{noun}} to show meaningful
                                          patterns. You have {{current}} so far."
  Container is role="status" aria-live="polite"; the check + info glyphs are aria-hidden.

